  "description": "COZFAA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C144 H120 Cl2 Eu6 Li4 O20 Si12,2(C5 H12). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.458-3.956 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.55-115.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C144H120Cl2Eu6Li4O20Si12·2(C5H12). Article name explicitly identifies Eu(II), Eu(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
